you have to keep working.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.200
-Yeah, okay.
Oh, I understand.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.701
Ah.
I understand.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:38.701
-So, I thought Prosecco
would work well for me.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:39.901
-Oh, I love Prosecco.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.701
And you actually have
a little sip of it --

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.934
cheers -- for me.
-Yes, please.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.534
-And The Roots -- Prosecco.
Cheers, everybody.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.167
-Ahh.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.033
I hope it's cold.
-Ooh!

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:53.601
Yummy!
-Is it cold?

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.467
-It's perfectly cold.
-Okay.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:56.801
-Perfectly chilled.
-Okay.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.200
Whoopi Prosecco, I love it.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.801
And what was the bread
you brought?

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.334
You always bring us some
nice goods, baked goods.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.100
-Pane-- Panettone.
-Yes.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.701
-it's Christmas bread.
-It is!

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.567
You did!
You brought the Christmas

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.400
