00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.033
Oh.
Look at this.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.534
He loves you.
-Oh, I'm just gonna give you --

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:26.501
Oh, my goodness.
-I got nothing from that puppy.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.033
Get ov-- Get over here.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.934
Come here.
Give me this one, yeah.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.868
Come here.
-Ooh, child, that's a big --

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.167
-Wow.
Pbht!

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.534
-This is not a puppy at all.
Hi.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:35.968
-That is a puppy.
-That's what I'm -- pbht!

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.734
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.767
-Thank you.
Pbht!

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:40.934
That's what I wanted.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:44.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.067
-I know.
-Come here.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:48.167
I didn't want you doing anything
on the sweater.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.968
Oh, geez.
-Had a little bit of doggy poo.

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:53.334
But that's all right.
That's all right.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.033
I've got a little something,
too.

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.467
-All right, perfect.
Pfft!

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:57.767
-Aww.
-All right.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:59.501
Can we take our models?
Can someone take our --

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:01.334
Oh.
You're hopping up here again?

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.334
Here you go.
We can have our models

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.501
taken away.
-Thank you.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.667
-But thank you for being here.
-Wonderful.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.934
-You can clap, sure.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:11.567
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:15.334
-Oof. That was --
-Wow.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:18.601
-Oh, but it's
kind of late for this.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.667
-That one got sloppy,
that first one.

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:24.934
[ Laughter ]
I think that first one

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.767
had a little Prosecco
before it came out.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.067
-I think so.
I think so.

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.033
-Yeah, had a little Prosecco,
that first one.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.100
-Had a little wine
on its breath.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.767
-Yeah, it did have a little --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.767
I love that.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.000
Thank you
for having them out here.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.167
Thanks for always coming.

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.033
And congrats on the sweaters.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:41.567
You can get them
right now at Nordstrom,

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:42.701
ladies and gentlemen.
-Yes.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:48.267
-I have questions to ask you.
-Okay.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:51.734
-We've talked about this
on the show -- "Sister Act 3."

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.000
The people have spoken.
We want it.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.267
-Yeah.
-And you said,

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:56.868
"They're gonna get it."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:58.868
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:00.534
-And we're going to get it.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:03.133
-The script came in yesterday.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:05.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:08.601
Good?
-I really like it.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.501
You know, but it has a whole
lot of adults to go through.

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:14.968
So if they don't get in its way,

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.734
it could actually
be pretty good.

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.934
And I'm just saying, you know --

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:21.567
Did you ever see --
what was it --

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:23.834
"Batman," the TV show?
-Yes.

00:06:23.834 --> 00:06:25.434
-Remember when Batman and Robin

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:27.167
would be going up
the side of the wall?

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:28.667
-Yes.
-And suddenly a window

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.701
would open, and somebody would
stick their head out?

00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:32.701
-Yeah.
-Would you stick your head out

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:36.200
if we made a space for you
to just come and do it

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.934
for, like, a day?
-Yes! Are you kidding me?

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:40.400
-No.
-To be in "Sister Act 3"?

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.968
-Yeah.
-Of course I would do that!

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:44.234
I would do anything for you!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:46.634
I'd do anything -- I love you!
I would do anything for that.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.968
-Thank you.
-I love --

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:50.868
I just love
even the story behind it, too,

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.868
because you pitched a sequel.

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:53.934
And then, they were like --

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.200
the studio were like,
"Maybe not."

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.501
And then just
the people took over.

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:59.133
-And then people went berserk,
and I thank you so much.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.567
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:02.534
That's how you do it.
-That's how you do it.

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.400
-That's how you do it.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.634
Let's talk about your new film,
"Till."

00:07:06.634 --> 00:07:08.067
-"Till," yeah.

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:10.968
You produced this.
You star in this.

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:13.100
Man, oh, man,
the reviews are unbelievable.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.100
98% on Rotten Tomatoes.
-Right.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.334
And this is, uh --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:20.000
It's something
you've been working on.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.634
-We've been trying
to get this made,

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:25.534
and the gentleman who really
was at the forefront of this,

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:27.400
his name is Keith Beauchamp.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:34.567
And he knew Mamie Till Mobley,
and he had always hoped

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:38.234
we could get it done
before she passed.

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:39.868
But we weren't able to do it.

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:43.334
But the movie is so great.

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:44.968
And I just want to say
to everybody,

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:46.968
don't be afraid to go see it.

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:49.834
There's no --

00:07:49.834 --> 00:07:53.534
You will understand that
the violence isn't there.

00:07:53.534 --> 00:07:55.534
Because we don't need
to tell you what happened.

00:07:55.534 --> 00:07:57.133
You know what happened.

00:07:57.133 --> 00:08:01.501
But what you're seeing is a
relationship between a mother

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:06.667
who decides that the world needs
to see what was done to her son.

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:09.834
And it's the perspective
between a mother and a son.

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:12.501
And we all know mothers,
and we all know sons.

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:15.667
So, please, if you have
11-year-olds, 12-year-olds,

00:08:15.667 --> 00:08:17.534
it's good for them
because it's part of

00:08:17.534 --> 00:08:19.667
the history of the country.

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:22.601
We can't pretend
it didn't happen. It did.

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:26.133
But what it did was,
it began a movement

00:08:26.133 --> 00:08:28.868
like no other that we've seen.

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:30.167
So please go see it.

00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:33.667
And the woman that plays
Mrs. Mobley

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:37.567
just won the Gotham Award
for Best Actress.

00:08:37.567 --> 00:08:40.601
Her name is Danielle Deadwyler.
-She was phenomenal.

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:41.934
-She is --

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:45.100
I've never
seen a performance like this.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.701
She is --
It's just --

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:49.200
It's the best thing I think
I've ever seen from an actor.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.234
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:51.234 --> 00:08:52.601
-It's powerful.
It's amazing.

00:08:52.601 --> 00:08:54.934
And you got to be in it
with her.

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.801
-Yes.

00:08:56.801 --> 00:08:58.501
-Were you always
supposed to be in it?

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:01.667
I think you were just
producing it.

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:03.968
-This is how long ago
we started this.

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:08.400
When we started talking about
doing it and helping Keith,

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:12.200
Barbara Broccoli and Fred Zollo,
who did "Mississippi Burning"

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.000
and all these other films.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:16.367
And so we tried, I think,

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.634
for the last 12 years
to get it done.

00:09:18.634 --> 00:09:22.434
And everybody kept saying,
"No, nobody wants to see this.

00:09:22.434 --> 00:09:23.968
They know this.
Nobody wants --"

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:26.968
And we got really lucky.

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:29.667
And then we,
got a brilliant director,

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:32.367
who did such an amazing job...
-Had a vision.

00:09:32.367 --> 00:09:37.367
-...at making this family
and this incident

00:09:37.367 --> 00:09:39.801
part of your family.

00:09:39.801 --> 00:09:43.767
So that you recognize
that this kind of --

00:09:43.767 --> 00:09:48.300
What is it called? --
incipient -- this racism.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.834
When you see it
in its full-blown, ugly face,

00:09:52.834 --> 00:09:57.267
as we show you in the film,
what it does to people.

00:09:57.267 --> 00:09:59.901
When you see it like that,
you begin to recognize

00:09:59.901 --> 00:10:02.334
that it could happen
to any of us.

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:06.133
That this could happen
to any of us at any time.

00:10:06.133 --> 00:10:09.300
So please, do me a favor.
This --

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.667
The performances are so good
that, I tell you,

00:10:13.667 --> 00:10:16.534
you will not be angry at me.
-Yeah.

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:18.467
-You won't be pissed at me
when you see this.

00:10:18.467 --> 00:10:22.000
-No, no.
-It's a fabulous film.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.734
-We love you, bud.
I'm so happy you did this.

00:10:23.734 --> 00:10:24.734
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:26.567
Here's Whoopi Goldberg
in "Till."

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:27.767
Take a look at this.

00:10:27.767 --> 00:10:29.634
-We've never been apart
this long.

00:10:31.467 --> 00:10:34.133
-He's just going
to see his cousins.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:36.334
It's not a bad thing for him
to know where he come from.

00:10:36.334 --> 00:10:39.067
-Chicago is all
he needs to know.

00:10:39.067 --> 00:10:40.767
I don't want him seeing himself

00:10:40.767 --> 00:10:44.334
the way those people
are seen down there.

00:10:44.334 --> 00:10:47.801
-Those people like me?

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:52.334
-Even you left Mississippi,
Mama.

00:10:52.334 --> 00:10:56.501
-Mamie, Bo is growing up.

00:10:56.501 --> 00:10:58.567
You gonna have to let him go.

00:11:01.334 --> 00:11:02.901
All right, I know that face.

00:11:02.901 --> 00:11:05.934
That is the face of
"Mama, mind your business

00:11:05.934 --> 00:11:07.400
and go home."
Where's my pocketbook?

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:08.701
-Mm-hmm.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.534
-Come on.
That's Whoopi Goldberg.

00:11:10.534 --> 00:11:11.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:11.834 --> 00:11:15.267
"Till" is in theaters right now,
everyone.

00:11:15.267 --> 00:11:16.801
Please go see this film.

